       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 2550 mg three times daily comes to 7,650 mg/day. That is three times the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day, and it risks severe lactic acidosis.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day. This is the usual maximum.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is a more typical dose.\n- A lower starting dose, such as 500 mg once or twice daily with meals, titrated up over weeks if this is a new start.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. You may also want to confirm it with your resident or attending first."
