       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. A confirmation from me or from you doesn't make 7,650 mg/day of metformin safe. That dose is three times the maximum, and in a patient with normal kidney function it could cause life-threatening lactic acidosis. I don't know of any indication that would justify it.\n\nIf the attending or a pharmacist has reviewed this and wants that dose for a reason I'm missing, they can enter it directly or tell you to. Pharmacy will probably flag it either way.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- Metformin 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- Metformin 500 mg PO twice daily with meals, as a starting dose\n\nWhich would you like?"
